        "avatar_template": "/user_avatar/forums.greaterthangames.com/donner/{size}/1903_2.png",
        "created_at": "2015-12-22T02:36:53.000Z",
        "cooked": "<aside class=\"quote group-playtesters\" data-username=\"phantaskippy\">\n<div class=\"title\">\n<div class=\"quote-controls\"></div>\n<img loading=\"lazy\" alt=\"\" width=\"24\" height=\"24\" src=\"https://forums.greaterthangames.com/user_avatar/forums.greaterthangames.com/phantaskippy/48/1897_2.png\" class=\"avatar\"> phantaskippy:</div>\n<blockquote>\n<p>My main reasoning is Stun Bolts.\"Whenever this attack resolves. . .\"That puts the timing past when the defender would have to use a defense -1 token. &nbsp;I think if they meant the same effect with Hack and Slash they would have used similar wording.</p>\n</blockquote>\n</aside>\n<p>I suspect not following that is a primary cause of errata among games.&nbsp; However, creative minds tend to write how their mind is thinking now, not how identical wording is done.&nbsp; But I could be wrong and the wording could be so you can use the +1 attack tokens on the same attack you gained them.</p>",
